        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This sounds great. (Though I'd consider f+ private)\nIn my worlds, I want to let players tailor the experience to suit their needs. But I **can't** do that, because a random player might join and press *all the buttons,* ruining the experience for everyone.\nI could... introduce a passcode system? Or add a whitelist for whom I trust? But that just seems sub-par.\nBeing able to detect whether an instance is public would solve this issue. We would be able to give players more control, without compromising on the experience of publics.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
